  <p>*Updated November 16, 2026, to include residents of Australia.</p>
<h4 id=3D"kiroween-2026-the-hackathon-official-rules">Kiroween 2026 (the =
=E2=80=9CHackathon=E2=80=9D) Official Rules</h4>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Rules translations:</strong> <a href=3D"https://kiroween.devpost=
.com/details/rules-translations">Bahasa Indonesia</a></p>
<p>NO PURCHASE OR PAYMENT NECESSARY TO ENTER OR WIN. A PURCHASE OR PAYMENT =
WILL NOT INCREASE YOUR CHANCES OF WINNING.&nbsp;</p>
<p>SUBMISSION OF ANY ENTRY CONSTITUTES AGREEMENT TO THESE OFFICIAL RULES AS=
 A CONTRACT BETWEEN ENTRANT (AND EACH INDIVIDUAL MEMBER OF ENTRANT), THE HA=
CKATHON SPONSOR, AND DEVPOST.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h5 id=3D"1-dates-and-timing">1. Dates and Timing</h5>
<p><strong>Registration Period</strong>: October 13, 2026 (8:30 am Pacific =
Time) =E2=80=93 December 4, 2026 (2:00 pm Pacific Time) (=E2=80=9CRegistrat=
ion Period=E2=80=9D).</p>
<p><strong>Submission Period</strong>: October 30, 2026 (9:00 am Pacific Ti=
me) =E2=80=93 December 4, 2026 (2:00 pm Pacific Time) (=E2=80=9CSubmission =
Period=E2=80=9D).</p>
<p>No extensions will be granted. Late Submissions will not be accepted.</p=
>
<p><strong>Judging Period</strong>: December 16, 2026 (1:00 pm Pacific Time=
) =E2=80=93 January 29, 2027 (1:00 pm Pacific Time) (=E2=80=9CJudging Perio=
d=E2=80=9D).</p>
<p><strong>Winners Announced</strong>: On or around February 3, 2027 (9:00 =
am Pacific Time).</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h5 id=3D"2-sponsor-and-administrator-promotional-entities">2. Sponsor and =
Administrator (=E2=80=9CPromotional Entities=E2=80=9D)</h5>
<p><strong>Sponsor</strong>: Amazon Web Services, 2121 7th Ave, Seattle, Wa=
shington 98121, United States</p>
<p><strong>Administrator</strong>: Devpost, Inc. (=E2=80=9CDevpost=E2=80=9D=
), 250 Broadway, Floor 24, New York, NY 10007</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h5 id=3D"3-eligibility">3. Eligibility</h5>
<p><strong>The Hackathon IS open to</strong>:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Individuals who are at least the age of majority where they reside as o=
f the time of entry (=E2=80=9CEligible Individuals=E2=80=9D);</li>
<li>Teams of Eligible Individuals, maximum 3 participants per team (=E2=80=
=9CTeams=E2=80=9D); and</li>
<li>Organizations (including corporations, not-for-profit corporations and =
other nonprofit organizations, limited liability companies, partnerships, a=
nd other legal entities) that exist and have been organized or incorporated=
 at the time of entry.</li>
</ul>
<p>(the above are collectively, =E2=80=9CEntrants=E2=80=9D)</p>
<p>An Eligible Individual may join more than one Team or Organization and a=
n Eligible Individual who is part of a Team or Organization may also enter =
the Hackathon on an individual basis. If a Team or Organization is entering=
 the Hackathon, they must appoint and authorize one individual (the =E2=80=
=9CRepresentative=E2=80=9D) to represent, act, and enter a Submission, on t=
heir behalf. By entering a Submission on behalf of a Team or Organization y=
ou represent and warrant that you are the Representative authorized to act =
on behalf of your Team or Organization.</p>
<p><strong>The Hackathon IS NOT open to</strong>:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Individuals who are residents of, or Organizations domiciled in, a coun=
try, state, province or territory where the laws of the United States or lo=
cal law prohibits participating or receiving a prize in the Hackathon (incl=
uding, but not limited to the province of Quebec, Argentina, Brazil, Italy,=
 Philippines, Russia, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Belarus, the region o=
f Crimea, the so-called Donetsk People=E2=80=99s Republic region (DNR), the=
 so-called Luhansk People=E2=80=99s Republic region (LNR), the United Arab =
Emirates and any other country which is comprehensively sanctioned by the U=
.S. Treasury=E2=80=99s Office of Foreign Assets Control)&nbsp;</li>
<li>Organizations involved with the design, production, paid promotion, exe=
cution, or distribution of the Hackathon, including the Sponsor and Adminis=
trator (=E2=80=9CPromotional Entities=E2=80=9D).</li>
<li>Employees, representatives and agents** of such Promotion Entities, and=
 all members of their immediate family or household*</li>
<li>Any other individual involved with the design, production, promotion, e=
xecution, or distribution of the Hackathon, and each member of their immedi=
ate family or household*</li>
<li>Any Judge (defined below), or company or individual that employs a Judg=
e</li>
<li>Any parent company, subsidiary, or other affiliate*** of any organizati=
on described above</li>
<li>Any other individual or organization whose participation in the Hackath=
on would create, in the sole discretion of the Sponsor and/or Administrator=
, a real or apparent conflict of interest&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><em>*The members of an individual=E2=80=99s immediate family include the=
 individual=E2=80=99s spouse, children and stepchildren, parents and steppa=
rents, and siblings and stepsiblings. The members of an individual=E2=80=99=
s household include any other person that shares the same residence as the =
individual for at least three (3) months out of the year.&nbsp;</em></p>
<p><em>**Agents include individuals or organizations that in creating a Sub=
mission to the Hackathon, are acting on behalf of, and at the direction of,=
 a Promotion Entity through a contractual or similar relationship.</em></p>
<p><em>***An affiliate is: (a) an organization that is under common control=
, sharing a common majority or controlling owner, or common management; or =
(b) an organization that has a substantial ownership in, or is substantiall=
y owned by the other organization.</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h5 id=3D"4-how-to-enter">4. How To Enter</h5>
<p>Entrants may enter by visiting kiroween.devpost.com (=E2=80=9CHackathon =
Website=E2=80=9D) and following the below steps:</p>
<ul>
<li>Register for the Hackathon on the Hackathon Website by clicking the =E2=
=80=9CJoin Hackathon=E2=80=9D button. To complete registration, sign up to =
create a free Devpost account, or log in with an existing Devpost account. =
This will enable you to receive important updates and to create your Submis=
sion.</li>
<li>Entrants will obtain access to the required developer tools/platform an=
d complete a Project described below in Project Requirements. Use of the de=
veloper tools will be subject to the license agreement related thereto. Ent=
ry in the Hackathon constitutes consent for the Sponsor and Devpost to coll=
ect and maintain an entrant=E2=80=99s personal information for the purpose =
of operating and publicizing the Hackathon. AWS handles your information in=
 accordance with <a href=3D"https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/" target=3D"_bla=
nk" rel=3D"noopener">AWS Privacy Notice</a>.</li>
<li>Entrants acknowledge and agree that the availability of certain feature=
s, AI models, and functionalities within Kiro may vary by geographic region=
. Entrants are solely responsible for reviewing and complying with all appl=
icable regional restrictions, including without limitation any restrictions=
 on AI model availability and usage, as published on the official Kiro webs=
ite (https://kiro.dev) or such other URL as may be designated by the Sponso=
r from time to time (collectively, the "Regional Restrictions"). The Sponso=
r makes no representation or warranty that all Kiro features, AI models, or=
 functionalities will be available to Entrants in all jurisdictions. Entran=
ts' use of Kiro in connection with this Hackathon is subject to, and condit=
ioned upon compliance with, all such Regional Restrictions. Any Hackathon s=
ubmission that relies on features or models not available in the Entrant's =
region shall be the sole responsibility of the Entrant, and the Sponsor sha=
ll have no liability arising from or related to any such regional limitatio=
ns.</li>
