<p><strong>Project Requirements</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>What to Create</strong>: Entrants must build a working software =
application using <a href=3D"http://kiro.dev/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noo=
pener">Kiro</a> (IDE, CLI, Web, and/or Kiro Crew) and submit it into one of=
 the following categories (each a =E2=80=9CProject=E2=80=9D). Insufficient =
use of Kiro will result in disqualification at the Judges=E2=80=99 sole dis=
cretion.</p>
<ul>
<li>Resurrection: Bring your favorite dead technology back to life. Reimagi=
ne obsolete tech with today=E2=80=99s innovations or solving tomorrow's pro=
blems.</li>
<li>Frankenstein: Stitch together a chimera of technologies into one app. B=
ring together seemingly incompatible elements to build something unexpected=
ly powerful.</li>
<li>Skeleton Crew: Build a skeleton code template lean enough to be clear b=
ut flexible enough to support various use cases. Show us its versatility wi=
th two distinct applications from your foundation.</li>
<li>Costume Contest: Build any app but show us a haunting user interface th=
at=E2=80=99s polished and unforgettable. Bring in spooky design elements th=
at enhance your app=E2=80=99s function.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Functionality</strong>: The Project must be capable of being suc=
cessfully installed and running consistently on the platform for which it i=
s intended and must function as depicted in the video and/or expressed in t=
he text description.</p>
<p><strong>Platforms</strong>: A submitted Project must run on the platform=
 for which it is intended and which is specified in the Submission Requirem=
ents.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>New Projects Only</strong>: Projects must be newly created by th=
e Entrant after the start of the Hackathon Submission Period. Participants =
may use standard development resources, including frameworks, libraries, st=
arter templates, but must disclose any other pre-existing code or work inco=
rporated into the Project. The work described and submitted must have been =
built during the Submission Period.</p>
<p><strong>Third Party Integrations</strong>: If a Project integrates any t=
hird-party SDK, APIs and/or data, Entrant must be authorized to use them in=
 accordance with any terms and conditions or licensing requirements of the =
tool.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
