<h5 id=3D"6-judges-criteria">6. Judges &amp; Criteria</h5>
<p>Sponsor and Administrator reserve the sole right to determine the eligib=
ility and judging methodologies for all submissions. This process may utili=
ze expert panels, peer review, automated AI-driven analysis, or any combina=
tion thereof to ensure efficient, fair, and objective evaluation. Eligible =
submissions will be evaluated by a panel of judges selected by the Sponsor =
(the =E2=80=9CJudges=E2=80=9D). Judges may be employees of the Sponsor or t=
hird parties, may or may not be listed individually on the Hackathon Websit=
e, and may change before or during the Judging Period. Judging may take pla=
ce in one or more rounds with one or more panels of Judges, at the discreti=
on of the Sponsor.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Stage One</strong>) The first stage will determine via pass/fail=
 whether the ideas meet a baseline level of viability, in that the Project =
reasonably fits the theme and reasonably applies the required tools feature=
d in the Hackathon.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Stage Two</strong>) All Submissions that pass Stage One will be =
evaluated in Stage Two based on the following equally weighted criteria (th=
e =E2=80=9CJudging Criteria=E2=80=9D):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<strong>Potential Impact</strong> (20% - 10 points)<br>Does the project mak=
e a credible case for solving a real problem for a real audience? Does the =
solution address that problem based on what=E2=80=99s demonstrated? How use=
ful, intuitive, and accessible is it? Would someone actually use this?</li>
<li>
<strong>Technological Implementation</strong> (20% - 10 points)<br>How thor=
oughly and skillfully does the project use Kiro? Was there a thoughtful str=
ategy to AI development? Was a variety of Kiro tools used impactfully? Does=
 the project show a deep understanding of Kiro features? Was there experime=
ntation?</li>
<li>
<strong>Design</strong> (20% - 10 points)<br>Does the project deliver a com=
plete, coherent product experience, not just a technical proof of concept? =
Is the design intuitive, polished, and intentional?</li>
<li>
<strong>Innovation/Idea</strong> (20% - 10 points)<br>How creative and nove=
l is the concept, and does the project differ from existing concepts? Are a=
ny unusual technologies or public resources (like datasets) leveraged or co=
mbined in a unique way?</li>
<li>
<strong>Presentation</strong> (20% - 10 points)<br>Does the video clearly d=
emonstrate the project working end-to-end? Does the pitch communicate what =
problem is solved, who it=E2=80=99s for, and why it matters? Is the overall=
 presentation easy to follow? Is the presentation creative and memorable?</=
li>
</ul>
<p>The scores from the Judges will determine the potential winners of the a=
pplicable prizes. The Entrant(s) that are eligible for a Prize, and whose S=
ubmissions earn the highest overall scores based on the applicable Judging =
Criteria, will become potential winners of that Prize.&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Overall Prizes will be awarded to the highest-scoring eligible Submissi=
ons across all categories.</li>
<li>Category Prizes will be awarded to the highest-scoring eligible Submiss=
ion in each category indicated in the Project Submission based on the same =
Judging Criteria.</li>
<li>Best Startup Project Bonus Prize will be awarded to the highest-scoring=
 eligible Submission with an eligible Startup profile and required details =
shared in the Project Submission.</li>
<li>Best Ghost of Kiroween Past Bonus Prize will be awarded to the highest-=
scoring eligible Submission that indicates 2025 Kiroween participation and =
is verified by Devpost.</li>
<li>Best Kiro Crew App Bonus Prizes will be evaluated by the Kiro team from=
 among the top 50 eligible Submissions that include a Kiro Crew app GitHub =
repo link. The top Kiro Crew app will be evaluated at the sole discretion o=
f the Kiro team based on the value/usefulness and technical innovation/idea=
.</li>
<li>Best Student Project for each category will be awarded to the highest-s=
coring eligible Submission in the category indicated in the Project Submiss=
ion and also includes eligible student details in the Submission.&nbsp;</li=
>
<li>Best Demo Bonus Prize will be awarded to the highest-scoring eligible S=
ubmission in the Presentation criterion that is also in the top 10% of over=
all eligible Submission scores. Any ties will be reviewed according to the =
Tie Breaking rules for the Presentation criterion alone.</li>
<li>Blog Post Bonus Prizes will be awarded to the top 100 highest-scoring e=
ligible Submissions that included a public blog post about Kiro published d=
uring the hackathon submission period with the required mention of Kiroween=
 Hackathon 2026. If fewer than 100 Submissions qualify, leftover prizes wil=
l not be awarded.</li>
<li>Social Blitz Bonus Prizes will be awarded to 5 eligible Submissions tha=
t include links to a public social post with the required #KiroweenHackatho=
n26 hashtag at the beginning of the post. The Kiro team will evaluate based=
 on the quality of the post content (original thoughts vs AI writing, inter=
esting insights or learnings about Kiro), the quality of any post assets (i=
mages or videos), and select the top 5 at their sole discretion. Social pro=
files that do not match other submission details may be disqualified at the=
 Promotional Entities=E2=80=99 sole discretion.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tie Breaking</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>If two or more Submissions are tied, the Judges will re-evaluate the tie=
d Submissions from scratch using a 20-point scoring maximum for each criter=
ion instead of the original 10 points. If the tie persists, this process wi=
ll repeat with a +10-point maximum for each criterion for each round of tie=
-breaking required until a winner emerges.</p>
